        {
          "category": "workflow-guidance",
          "title": "Frontend 'full workflow' mandates a design/review/screenshot process that the factory smoke task explicitly forbids",
          "detail": "The ui-workflow reference classifies any new page as 'full workflow', requiring storage/ui-workflow/<feature> design.md, an independent design review, browser screenshots and an acceptance review. This task is an intentionally trivial pipeline smoke test and explicitly states that screenshots, reports and QA are factory-owned and that no style refinement or architecture work is expected. Following the skill literally would create throwaway artifacts and reviewer subagents for a 30-line counter page.",
